    "before": {
      "title": "Beef Stroganoff Crepes with Mushrooms",
      "excerpt": "Thin crepes filled with strips of beef and mushrooms in a creamy Stroganoff-style sauce, ready in just over an hour.",
      "summary": "This dish combines two classics from different culinary traditions: the French crepe and Russian-born Stroganoff sauce, made with beef strips, mushrooms and a creamy base. Together they make thin crepes wrapped around a juicy, well-seasoned filling, perfect as a weeknight main course or to impress at dinner. The secret is browning the beef well in batches, without crowding the pan, and adding the cream over low heat so the sauce turns silky without splitting. Serve hot, freshly assembled, with fresh parsley on top.",
      "notes": "<h3>Tips</h3><ul><li>Let the batter rest for 30 minutes before cooking the crepes: they turn out thinner and flip with fewer tears.</li><li>Cut the beef into thin strips and brown it in batches: if the pan is crowded, the meat releases water and steams instead of browning.</li><li>The first crepe usually comes out worse; use it to adjust the heat and the amount of fat in the pan.</li></ul><h3>Substitutions</h3><ul><li>Heavy cream: creme fraiche or sour cream.</li><li>Beef broth: chicken or vegetable broth.</li></ul><h3>Storage</h3><p>Store the crepes and the filling separately in the fridge for up to 3 days. Reheat the filling over low heat and add a little broth if it thickens too much.</p><h3>Source</h3><p class=\"md-sources\">Source: <a href=\"https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/safe-minimum-internal-temperature\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">USDA FSIS, safe minimum internal temperatures</a>.</p>",
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Mix the dry ingredients",
          "content": "Mix the flour, sugar and salt."
        },
        {
          "title": "Make the batter",
          "content": "Beat the eggs, add the milk and melted butter, and combine with the dry ingredients until you have a lump-free batter.",
          "image_alt": "Crepe batter whisked in a glass bowl",
          "image_url": "/recetas/creep-stroganoff/paso-02.webp"
        },
        {
          "title": "Cook the crepes",
          "content": "Cook thin crepes, 1 to 2 minutes per side, in a lightly greased pan, and set them aside.",
          "image_alt": "Thin crepe browning in a pan",
          "image_url": "/recetas/creep-stroganoff/paso-03.webp"
        },
        {
          "title": "Saute the onion and garlic",
          "content": "Melt the butter for the filling and saute the onion and garlic."
        },
        {
          "title": "Brown the beef",
          "content": "Add the beef and brown it for 3 to 4 minutes; add the mushrooms and cook until tender.",
          "image_alt": "Beef strips and mushrooms browning in the pan",
          "image_url": "/recetas/creep-stroganoff/paso-05.webp"
        },
        {
          "title": "Add the flour",
          "content": "Sprinkle in the flour and stir for a minute so it blends in without lumps."
        },
        {
          "title": "Make the sauce",
          "content": "Add the broth little by little, stirring, and cook until the sauce thickens.",
          "image_alt": "Creamy mushroom and beef sauce ready in the pan",
