            "q": "What cut is bondiola?",
            "a": "It is a marbled pork neck cut suited to slow cooking. Ask your butcher for pork neck; names differ between countries."
          },
          {
            "q": "How long does a 2 kg pork neck take?",
            "a": "Start checking after about 2 hours covered at 160 °C (320 °F). If not tender, continue covered with liquid in the pan; thickness also matters. Finally uncover and brown for 15–20 minutes at 200 °C (400 °F)."
