            "a": "About 16 hours including resting: 8 to 12 hours of marinating and soaking the night before, about 60 minutes of prep and 3 hours in the oven, plus 20 minutes of rest.",
            "q": "How long does lechona take to make at home?"
          },
          {
            "a": "Yes. The marinade and the soaking are done the day before. You can also bake it fully, refrigerate it and reheat it until the center reaches 74 °C (165 °F), reviving the skin for 10 minutes at 200 °C (400 °F).",
            "q": "Can I prepare it a day ahead?"
          },
          {
            "a": "Cook it only to three-quarters and mix the filling with pea cooking liquid so it stays moist. In the oven it absorbs the pork juices and finishes cooking.",
            "q": "How do I keep the rice from turning hard or dry?"
          },
          {
            "a": "Arepa and ají are the usual companions. A squeeze of fresh lime also works well with the pork.",
