      "summary": "This home-style Colombian lechona is baked in a deep dish with pork, yellow peas, rice and skin-on pork belly. It serves 8 without stuffing a whole pig. It is a rice-based adaptation: traditional Tolima lechona contains pork and peas, without rice.\n\nStart the night before: soak the peas and refrigerate the marinated pork for 8–12 hours. The next day, cook the peas, partially cook the rice and assemble the dish. Allow roughly 16 hours 20 minutes overall when counting a 12-hour overnight rest, preparation, baking and final resting.\n\nKeep the skin facing up, dry and free of wet marinade, and moisten the filling with the reserved cooking liquid. Use a deep dish with headroom and check that the center of the filling reaches 74 °C (165 °F) before serving.",
      "notes": "<h3>Tips</h3><ul><li>Crisp skin depends on dryness: do not coat it with the paste, and leave it uncovered in the fridge.</li><li>Cut the shoulder into similar-sized pieces so it cooks evenly.</li><li>The filling touches raw meat while baking: use a thermometer and confirm at least 74 °C (165 °F) in the center before taking it out.</li><li>Do not cook the rice fully before assembling; it would overcook in the dish.</li></ul><h3>Substitutions</h3><ul><li>Lard: vegetable oil works, with less flavor.</li><li>Banana leaves: line the dish with parchment and cover with foil; some aroma is lost.</li><li>Cebolla larga: scallions or spring onions, in the same amount.</li><li>Achiote: sweet paprika, for color.</li><li>Pork belly without skin: the recipe works, but there will be no crackling.</li></ul><h3>Storage</h3><p>Cool leftovers and refrigerate them within 2 hours, in closed containers. They keep for 3 to 4 days and should be reheated until the center reaches 74 °C (165 °F). You can freeze portions for up to 3 months. The skin loses its crunch in storage: revive it for 10 minutes in a 200 °C (400 °F) oven.</p><p class=\"md-sources\">Sources: <a href=\"https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/safe-temperature-chart\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">USDA FSIS, safe minimum internal temperatures</a>; <a href=\"https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/leftovers-and-food-safety\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">USDA FSIS, leftovers and food safety</a>.</p><p>References: <a href=\"https://tolima.gov.co/noticias/442-lechona-tolimense-manjar-de-dioses-que-deleita-los-paladares-de-propios-y-visitantes-en-epocas-de-festividades-de-mitad-de-ano\">Gobernación del Tolima</a>.</p><h3>More meat recipes for another meal</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/en/chorizo-santarosano/\">Homemade Santarrosano Chorizo: Fresh Colombian Sausage</a></li><li><a href=\"/en/pork-bondiola-reci